+    by a patch generator, and each patch is optionally post-processed by a transform. The patch generator is usually
+    :py:class:`PatchIter`, but any callable that takes one image item and yields tuples whose first element is the
+    patch and whose optional second element is its coordinates can be used.
+
+    The coordinates are an integer array with one row per dimension of the image, including the channel dimension.
+    Each row holds ``[start, stop]`` of that dimension for the patch, in the original unpadded image frame. For a
+    one-channel 2D image the coordinates of a patch have shape (3, 2).
+
